alled by StartUp and Main whenever a new directory is   **	to be checked for scripts.  Scripts found are added to    **	list already begun by Check4Scripts.	                  **			                  **   3)  Alphabetize - Always called before displaying a new script list.      **	This is the routine that locks down the lists, tells us   **	where it is located, and how many members it contains.    **			                  **   4)  CheckMsgCenter - Called once by StartUp to determine if the user      **	requested OPENing any of the script files in which case   **	they are added to the list, if not currently there, and   **	marked "selected" in the customized installation display. **			                  ** * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * ** * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *AddScripts	Procname Export** Description:	AddScripts searches the specified directory for SCRIPT*	files.  If scripts are found, they are added to the*	existing script list.  (The list is not re-alphabetized.)**        NOTE:	Old scripts  = filetype $04, auxtype $0000, contains "SCRIPT"*	Scripts V1.n = filetype $B0, auxtype $0017, contains "SCRIPT"** Inputs:	X and Y-reg contain pointer to FULL pathname of directory*	to scan, a GS/OS Class 1 output string.** Outputs:	c-flag clear: no errors*	c-flag set: A-reg contains error and user has been alerted.*	v-flag clear: no scripts added*	v-flag set: scripts were added to the list.* External Refs:	Import Aux_Type	Import ColonBuf	Import cVersion	Import DeReference	Import DialogFlag	Import Error	Import File_Type	Import Get_Dir_Parms	Import GStrConcat	Import GStrResize	Import GStrToC1Inp	Import InitHeapsort	Import messageHandle	Import NameBuffer	Import oScriptNameField	Import PointerSize	Import ScriptFileHdl	Import ScriptListBuilt	Import ScriptListCtlHdl	Import ScriptListHdl	Import ScriptListSize	Import Sort	Import WindowSetupComplete** Entry Points:	Export Alphabetize	Export CheckMsgCenter	Export NoCaseCompare8bit	Export UpperCase8bit** Side Effects:	This routine will build a list of pointers and ScriptName*	strings for the List Manager (see ControlData) and a list*	of script filenames for later script execution.** * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *OldScriptType	equ $04	; Script filetype (ASCII text)NewScriptType	equ $B0	; APW Source fileScriptAux	equ $0017	; APW Language (OldScript)	Eject	phb	phk	plb	stz ScriptAddFlag; Store the Directory's pathname pointer (GS/OS Class 1 output string buffer).	stx <PathBuf	sty <PathBuf+2; Open the directory and initialize Get_Dir_Parms.	inx	; Point to strings length word	bne @0001	iny@0001	inx	bne @0002	iny@0002	stx Open_Path	sty Open_Path+2	jsl GSOS	dc.w Open	dc.l OpenParms	bcc @continue	jsl error	; inform the user	clc	; then pretend there's no error	bra ScriptOops@continue	lda OpenParms+2	sta Get_Dir_Parms+2	lda #0001	sta Get_Dir_Parms+6	; (base)	sta Get_Dir_Parms+8	; (displacement)	jsr AddColon; Store the pathname's length (so we can back up to the directory's pathname; after each script filename concatenation).	ldy #0002	lda [<PathBuf],y	sta DirPathLength; In a loop call Get_Dir_EntryScriptSearchLoop	jsl GSOS	; Call GS/OS to...	dc.w Get_Dir_Entry	; ...get a directory entry	dc.l Get_Dir_Parms	bcc CheckScriptEntry	cmp #EndOfDir	; No more entries?	bne ScriptOops	brl AddScriptsDoneScriptOops	brl ScriptExit	; Pass errors on; Check the entry to determine if it is a legitimate script fileCheckScriptEntry	ldy #0002	lda DirPathLength	; Put directory's length word back	sta [<PathBuf],y	jsr CheckEntry	bcs ScriptSearchLoop	Eject; It is a legitimate script file!  Make sure it isn't already in the list.; (The user may have re-inserted a volume that was previously off-line.);       Initialize variables.  If accessing the SCRIPTS folder failed or it;       co